(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 55, 'The descendants of Solomon"s servants: Sotai, Hassophereth, Peruda,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 56, 'Jaalah, Darkon, Giddel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 57, 'Shephatiah, Hattil, Pochereth-hazzebaim, and Ami.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 58, 'All the temple servants and the descendants of Solomon"s servants were three hundred ninety-two.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 59, 'The following were those who came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer, though they could not prove their families or their descent, whether they belonged to Israel:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 60, 'the descendants of Delaiah, Tobiah, and Nekoda, six hundred fifty-two.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 61, 'Also, of the descendants of the priests: the descendants of Habaiah, Hakkoz, and Barzillai (who had married one of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called by their name).', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 62, 'These looked for their entries in the genealogical records, but they were not found there, and so they were excluded from the priesthood as unclean;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 63, 'the governor told them that they were not to partake of the most holy food, until there should be a priest to consult Urim and Thummim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 64, 'The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 65, 'besides their male and female servants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven; and they had two hundred male and female singers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 66, 'They had seven hundred thirty-six horses, two hundred forty-five mules,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 67, 'four hundred thirty-five camels, and six thousand seven hundred twenty donkeys.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 68, 'As soon as they came to the house of the LORD in Jerusalem, some of the heads of families made freewill offerings for the house of God, to erect it on its site.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 69, 'According to their resources they gave to the building fund sixty-one thousand darics of gold, five thousand minas of silver, and one hundred priestly robes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 2, 70, 'The priests, the Levites, and some of the people lived in Jerusalem and its vicinity; and the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants lived in their towns, and all Israel in their towns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"For he is good,  
for his steadfast love endures forever toward Israel."
And all the people responded with a great shout when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD was laid.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 3, 12, 'But many of the priests and Levites and heads of families, old people who had seen the first house on its foundations, wept with a loud voice when they saw this house, though many shouted aloud for joy,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 3, 13, 'so that the people could not distinguish the sound of the joyful shout from the sound of the people"s weeping, for the people shouted so loudly that the sound was heard far away.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"To King Artaxerxes: Your servants, the people of the province Beyond the River, send greeting. And now', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 12, 'may it be known to the king that the Jews who came up from you to us have gone to Jerusalem. They are rebuilding that rebellious and wicked city; they are finishing the walls and repairing the foundations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 13, 'Now may it be known to the king that, if this city is rebuilt and the walls finished, they will not pay tribute, custom, or toll, and the royal revenue will be reduced.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 14, 'Now because we share the salt of the palace and it is not fitting for us to witness the king"s dishonor, therefore we send and inform the king,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 15, 'so that a search may be made in the annals of your ancestors. You will discover in the annals that this is a rebellious city, hurtful to kings and provinces, and that sedition was stirred up in it from long ago. On that account this city was laid waste.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 16, 'We make known to the king that, if this city is rebuilt and its walls finished, you will then have no possession in the province Beyond the River."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 17, 'The king sent an answer: "To Rehum the royal deputy and Shimshai the scribe and the rest of their associates who live in Samaria and in the rest of the province Beyond the River, greeting. And now', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 18, 'the letter that you sent to us has been read in translation before me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 19, 'So I made a decree, and someone searched and discovered that this city has risen against kings from long ago, and that rebellion and sedition have been made in it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 20, 'Jerusalem has had mighty kings who ruled over the whole province Beyond the River, to whom tribute, custom, and toll were paid.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 21, 'Therefore issue an order that these people be made to cease, and that this city not be rebuilt, until I make a decree.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 22, 'Moreover, take care not to be slack in this matter; why should damage grow to the hurt of the king?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 23, 'Then when the copy of King Artaxerxes" letter was read before Rehum and the scribe Shimshai and their associates, they hurried to the Jews in Jerusalem and by force and power made them cease.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 4, 24, 'At that time the work on the house of God in Jerusalem stopped and was discontinued until the second year of the reign of King Darius of Persia.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);





"O my God, I am too ashamed and embarrassed to lift my face to you, my God, for our iniquities have risen higher than our heads, and our guilt has mounted up to the heavens.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 7, 'From the days of our ancestors to this day we have been deep in guilt, and for our iniquities we, our kings, and our priests have been handed over to the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, to plundering, and to utter shame, as is now the case.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 8, 'But now for a brief moment favor has been shown by the LORD our God, who has left us a remnant, and given us a stake in his holy place, in order that he may brighten our eyes and grant us a little sustenance in our slavery.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 9, 'For we are slaves; yet our God has not forsaken us in our slavery, but has extended to us his steadfast love before the kings of Persia, to give us new life to set up the house of our God, to repair its ruins, and to give us a wall in Judea and Jerusalem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 10, '"And now, our God, what shall we say after this? For we have forsaken your commandments,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 11, 'which you commanded by your servants the prophets, saying, "The land that you are entering to possess is a land unclean with the pollutions of the peoples of the lands, with their abominations. They have filled it from end to end with their uncleanness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 12, 'Therefore do not give your daughters to their sons, neither take their daughters for your sons, and never seek their peace or prosperity, so that you may be strong and eat the good of the land and leave it for an inheritance to your children forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 13, 'After all that has come upon us for our evil deeds and for our great guilt, seeing that you, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserved and have given us such a remnant as this,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 14, 'shall we break your commandments again and intermarry with the peoples who practice these abominations? Would you not be angry with us until you destroy us without remnant or survivor?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(15, 'Ezr', 'Ezra', 9, 15, 'O LORD, God of Israel, you are just, but we have escaped as a remnant, as is now the case. Here we are before you in our guilt, though no one can face you because of this."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


At the time, I was cupbearer to the king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);






