(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 58, 'of Jaala, of Darkon, of Giddel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 59, 'of Shephatiah, of Hattil, of Pochereth-hazzebaim, of Amon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 60, 'All the temple servants and the descendants of Solomon"s servants were three hundred ninety-two.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 61, 'The following were those who came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer, but they could not prove their ancestral houses or their descent, whether they belonged to Israel:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 62, 'the descendants of Delaiah, of Tobiah, of Nekoda, six hundred forty-two.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 63, 'Also, of the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, of Hakkoz, of Barzillai (who had married one of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 64, 'These sought their registration among those enrolled in the genealogies, but it was not found there, so they were excluded from the priesthood as unclean;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 65, 'the governor told them that they were not to partake of the most holy food, until a priest with Urim and Thummim should come.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 66, 'The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 67, 'besides their male and female slaves, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven; and they had two hundred forty-five singers, male and female.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 68, 'They had seven hundred thirty-six horses, two hundred forty-five mules,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 69, 'four hundred thirty-five camels, and six thousand seven hundred twenty donkeys.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 70, 'Now some of the heads of ancestral houses contributed to the work. The governor gave to the treasury one thousand darics of gold, fifty basins, and five hundred thirty priestly robes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 71, 'And some of the heads of ancestral houses gave into the building fund twenty thousand darics of gold and two thousand two hundred minas of silver.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 72, 'And what the rest of the people gave was twenty thousand darics of gold, two thousand minas of silver, and sixty-seven priestly robes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(16, 'Neh', 'Nehemiah', 7, 73, 'So the priests, the Levites, the gatekeepers, the singers, some of the people, the temple servants, and all Israel settled in their towns.
When the seventh month came--the people of Israel being settled in their towns--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Ezra Summons the People to Obey the Law');







